  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Research Workbench",
    "overview": "A quiet, precise research tool with forest navigation, a pale workspace and white editing surfaces. Compact sans-serif text, fine dividers and modest corners support repeated bench and desk work. Teal identifies interaction and calculation context; amber keeps uncertain inputs and historical limitations visible.\n\nThis is a scan of the implemented code, not a user-approved visual identity. The descriptive north star and palette names are provisional documentation language. The optional direction question was unanswered; no approved visual comp or QUALITY BAR card exists. Preserve the implemented system during routine maintenance and seek an explicit direction decision before treating its atmosphere as an approved brand commitment.\n\nSource of truth: src/styles.css and the React components, with the real Three.js scene in src/components/ReactorScene.jsx. The 11 October 2026 desktop, mobile, actual-default, notebook and evidence captures under .impeccable/review were opened for this documentation pass. QA and the bounded ship verdict are recorded separately; neither establishes physical geometry, biological performance or comprehensive accessibility validation.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Compact, readable research hierarchy with tabular numbers.",
      "Tonal separation and thin dividers rather than elevated cards.",
      "Visible units, evidence labels and original-source context.",
      "Responsive editing around a genuine, schematic 3D scene."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Evidence Label Rule",
        "body": "Every evidence color travels with a written status. A green tone alone never establishes that a value was measured.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Unit Rule",
        "body": "Keep a number next to its unit and preserve tabular numerals for values, tables and comparison scores.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat Surface Rule",
        "body": "Separate panels with fill and thin borders. The selected segmented item is the only implemented CSS shadow role.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do reuse the extracted forest, teal, neutral and amber roles with their textual meanings.",
      "Do retain the shared focus outline and stable accessible names when visible button text is hidden.",
      "Do keep units, qualifiers, provenance and assumptions beside readings and computed values.",
      "Do follow the implemented breakpoint behavior and keep the viewer before the inspector on small screens.",
      "Do preserve original photographs and drawings with captions, source IDs and a route to the original file."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't label this provisional visual direction as user-approved.",
